{
  "_README": [
    "Labeled evaluation set for scripts/ablation.py.",
    "",
    "IMPORTANT — READ BEFORE QUOTING ANY NUMBER FROM THIS:",
    "These labels were authored by hand against the 5-entry PLACEHOLDER",
    "deeplinks.json, not against Samsung's real ~575-entry catalog. With only",
    "five candidate screens, several actions have no correct answer and most",
    "others are trivially separable, so absolute accuracy here is close to",
    "meaningless. What this set IS good for right now: comparing configurations",
    "against each other on identical inputs, and catching regressions.",
    "",
    "When the real deeplinks.json lands, replace the retrieval cases with",
    "actions labeled against real deeplink URIs and re-run. The harness needs",
    "no changes.",
    "",
    "expected_deeplink: null means NO catalog entry is correct, so the system",
    "SHOULD abstain. Those cases are what make the confidence floor and the",
    "ambiguity margin measurable instead of just asserted."
  ],

  "retrieval_cases": [
